course: dictionary
lesson: 12089
title: Clumping: heavy steps and sticking lumps
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clumping is a word with two main meanings. It can describe heavy, noisy steps, like boots on a wooden floor. It can also describe things sticking together into lumps or groups.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Heavy boots came clumping up the wooden stairs» tells you the steps were slow, heavy and loud. «Wet sand starts clumping together» tells you the grains are sticking into lumps.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping in a simple word. Clumping up the stairs means walking heavily, so that fits. Clumping together means sticking into lumps, so that fits too. If your swap makes sense in the sentence, you have found the meaning.
fact: Clumping is a form of the verb clump: clump, clumps, clumped, clumping.
fact: Clumping can mean walking with slow, heavy, noisy steps.
fact: Clumping can also mean gathering together into a tight group or into lumps.
fact: A clump (noun) is a group of plants growing close together, or a lump of something.
fact: In stories, heavy boots and loud floors are clues for the steps meaning; in cooking, flour and sand are clues for the lumps meaning.
exercise: «The giant came clumping through the forest.» What does clumping mean here? | *Walking with heavy, noisy steps | Floating silently above the trees | Hiding behind a tree | Singing a happy song
exercise: «Add a little more water, or the wet flour will start clumping.» What does clumping mean here? | Drying out into dust | *Sticking together into lumps | Turning a bright red colour | Rising up high like bread
exercise: In «a clump of daisies grew by the gate», what does clump mean? | *A group of plants growing close together | A loud noise made by boots | A lump of hard cheese | A stone path
test: «Heavy boots came clumping down the stone steps.» What does clumping suggest? | Quiet, gentle tiptoeing | Dancing happily | *Heavy, loud steps | Flying quickly
test: «The mud was clumping on the bottoms of our shoes.» What does clumping mean here? | Being washed away | Drying into a smooth floor | Shining brightly | *Sticking together in lumps
exam: Mia says clumping only ever means walking. Is she right? | No, it means something very quiet | Yes, but only when boots are wet | *No, clumping can also mean things sticking together in lumps or groups | Yes, it only means walking
